How tiles work:\nThe map is built from 256×256 "slippy" tiles. Only the tiles for the area you're viewing are fetched — there is no bulk pre-download.\n\nBecause this device can't do HTTPS (not enough heap after Wi-Fi starts) and decodes JPEG far more cheaply than PNG, tiles come from the wadamesh proxy: it fetches the upstream PNG over HTTPS with an identifying User-Agent, re-encodes it as JPEG, and caches it. Your device then caches each tile to its own flash, so a tile is only downloaded once.\n\nUse Options → Reload tiles to re-download the tiles currently in view if one looks corrupted.	Sådan virker fliser:\nKortet er bygget af 256×256 "slippy"-fliser. Kun fliserne for det område, du ser, hentes — der er ingen samlet forhåndsdownload.\n\nFordi denne enhed ikke kan HTTPS (ikke nok heap, når Wi-Fi er startet) og afkoder JPEG langt billigere end PNG, kommer fliserne fra wadamesh-proxyen: den henter den oprindelige PNG over HTTPS med en identificerende User-Agent, koder den om til JPEG og gemmer den. Enheden gemmer derefter hver flise i sin egen flash, så en flise kun downloades én gang.\n\nBrug Indstillinger → Genindlæs fliser for at downloade de viste fliser igen, hvis en ser ødelagt ud.
